//  PETPORTS -- ASTERITE MINING SPARK
//
//  A COSMETIC BURST AT A TILE. It does no damage, changes no tile, and carries
//  no effect. Its entire job is to make a noise and throw some particles where
//  a unit's beam lands, once per swing.
//
//  WHY A PROJECTILE RATHER THAN THE UNIT'S OWN ANIMATOR.
//
//  animator.playSound needs the sound declared in a pool on the monstertype's
//  .animation, which would mean editing five or six chassis files for a
//  cosmetic -- and then editing all of them again for the next matmod that
//  wants different sounds. A projectile takes its sounds as a PARAMETER, which
//  means they can come off the matmod at runtime and nothing in this mod ever
//  names an asterite noise.
//
//  IT ALSO PUTS THE EFFECT AT THE TILE RATHER THAN AT THE UNIT, which is where
//  a player is looking. The unit may be eight tiles away.
//
//  SHIPPED DELIBERATELY INCOMPLETE, exactly like petports_watersprinkle.
//  actionOnReap is EMPTY here; the caster fills it per swing from what it read
//  off the matmod being mined:
//
//    world.spawnProjectile("petports_asteritespark", centre, entity.id(),
//      {0, 0}, false, {
//        actionOnReap = {
//          { action = "loop", count = <n>, body = {
//              { action = "particle", specification = <miningParticle> } } },
//          { action = "sound", options = <miningSounds> }
//        }
//      })
//
//  IF PARAMETER OVERRIDE DOES NOT REACH actionOnReap this becomes a silent
//  invisible projectile that lives a tenth of a second and does nothing, which
//  is the failure to watch for and is why the caster logs what it passed.
//
//  physics "statuspod" AND speed 0, copied from petports_medicburst for the
//  same reason it uses them: this is delivered where it is aimed and must not
//  fall, drift or bounce off the tile it is decorating.
//
//  THE SPRITE IS INTENTIONALLY BLANK. DO NOT "FIX" IT BY DRAWING SOMETHING.
//  Same argument petports_medicburst makes at length -- the projectile lives a
//  tenth of a second, so anything drawn here is a single-frame flash that
//  reads as a rendering glitch. THE VISUAL IS THE PARTICLE BURST, which is the
//  matmod's own miningParticle and therefore already looks like that ore.
//  OUR OWN BLANK, NOT A BORROWED ONE: todo.art.invisibleframe records what
//  happens when a hide depends on somebody else's empty frame.

{
	"projectileName" : "petports_asteritespark",

	"physics" : "statuspod",
	"bounces" : -1,
	"speed" : 0,

	//  A TENTH OF A SECOND, AND IT HAS TO STAY UNDER THE SWING PERIOD.
	//
	//  actionOnReap fires when the projectile DIES, so this is the delay
	//  between the swing and its noise. The unit swings every 0.25 s; at 0.1
	//  the burst reads as part of the swing that spawned it, and anything
	//  approaching 0.25 would start landing on top of the next one.
	"timeToLive" : 0.1,

	"image" : "petports_asteritespark.png",
	"animationCycle" : 0.1,
	"frameNumber" : 3,
	"damageKindImage" : "icon.png",

	"pointLight" : false,
	"emitters" : [ ],

	//  FILLED BY THE CASTER. See the header.
	"actionOnReap" : [ ],

	//  NO DAMAGE OF ANY KIND, and "hidden" so no floating number appears. A
	//  mining spark is scenery; it must never be able to hurt the unit that
	//  cast it, the player standing beside it, or the tile underneath.
	"power" : 0.0,
	"damageType" : "NoDamage",
	"damageKind" : "hidden"
}
